# Eddymurk Crab, {5}{U}{U}: "This spell costs {1} less to cast for each instant and sorcery card in your graveyard." On turn 1 Bot1 casts
# Lightning Bolt (an instant) and Duress (a sorcery), so two cards count; the Black Lotus sacrificed on turn 3 is an artifact in the graveyard
# and counts for nothing. On turn 3 Bot1 taps seven mana (Mountain {R}, Mox Jet {B}, Mox Sapphire {U}, Black Lotus {U}{U}{U}, Island {U}) and the
# Crab costs {3}{U}{U} = five, so two blue mana are left in the pool (the reduction of 2, not 1 and not 3). It is Bot1's own turn, so
# "enters tapped if it's not your turn" does not apply: the Crab is untapped. Bot2 controls no creatures, so its trigger has nothing to tap.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Jet
Lightning Bolt
Duress
Eddymurk Crab
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Island
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
